@topic stdlib.abi::x86_64::from_u64
title: -
summary: The x86-64 register word of an abi::U64, zero-extended: a value of 2^63 or more travels as the negative word v - 2^64; total.
index: stdlib
keywords: u64 to register; encode argument; syscall argument
related: stdlib.abi::x86_64::Register64 stdlib.abi::U64

== NOTES
The same 64 bits, read signed: to_int(from_u64(abi::u64(2^64 - 1))) is
-1. This is how the whole unsigned 64-bit domain reaches a register,
which register64 (signed) would reject.

